# Byte-exact fixtures. The orthology and residue-mapping inputs' sha256s are part of what their
# recordings pin (the snapshot_id is a sha256 over them, and genes map-residues reports each file's),
# so a CRLF checkout on Windows must not change them, as pyMzLib's .gitattributes marks them. They
# sit in tests/orthology/ and tests/map_residues/ rather than tests/fixtures/, so no path in the
# built package passes the 100 bytes a portable tarball can store.
tests/orthology/** -text
tests/map_residues/** -text
